      "prompt": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the same sunset lake and empty wooden pier in <Picture 1>, with boathouse on left, village, church and tree-covered hills. <Subject 2> is one fictional plesiosaur-like lake creature with dark moss-green wet pebbled skin, a single slender curved long neck, small elongated reptilian head, two dark eyes and closed mouth. Only neck, head and one low rounded back emerge; its large body stays submerged. <Picture 2> defines the intended LATER surfaced creature and its location; the beginning is the empty lake in <Picture 1>.\nsummary: A single lake creature physically surfaces beyond the empty pier.\nretention_analysis: Preserve the established geometry, lighting, subject identities and materials from the images. <Picture 1> is the exact first view.\ndetailed_description: Naturalistic cinematic live-action, stable exposure and coherent physical motion. [Shot 1] The camera remains locked in the exact wide view of <Picture 1> for one uninterrupted take. Initially the lake surface beyond the empty pier is calm and uninterrupted. A small circular ripple develops about fifteen metres beyond the end of the pier, slightly to the RIGHT. The ripple spreads, water bulges upward, then one dark-green reptilian head physically breaks the water surface. Its long curved neck rises steadily out of the water, dripping, followed by a single low rounded back at the waterline. The head rises about three metres above the water and turns gently toward the empty pier. Water rings expand around the submerged body; the creature settles buoyantly with its neck above water. Buildings, pier and hills stay fixed, with the same sunset illumination. The creature emerges from below the water in one spatially continuous movement.\noverall_soundscape: Water lapping, an increasing bubbling splash as the head breaks the surface, water dripping from the raised neck. Nobody speaks.\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A",
